Day 3 — Database Integration & Search Engine Layer

- Migrated project from CSV-based storage to a structured SQLite relational database (jobs.db)
- Designed database schema to store job postings with fields for title, company, location, URL, and description
- Integrated scraper with database layer to store job postings directly into SQLite
- Implemented SQL-based search functionality using multi-field filtering (title, company, location)
- Added duplicate prevention using unique job identifiers and INSERT OR IGNORE constraints
- Resolved real-world development issues including:
    -Virtual environment configuration issues (Windows PowerShell)
    - Package dependency conflicts
    - SQLite schema mismatch and datatype errors
    - Git synchronization issues between local and remote repository

Outcome:
Upgraded system from flat-file data storage to a queryable database-backed job search engine.
